== Effects ==
* {{e|Mom}}'s dismembered leg stomps on the enemy with the most health, dealing 300 damage and destroying obstacles in the area.
* If used in an empty room or during the {{e|Mom}} fight, the foot stomps Isaac instead, dealing a full heart of damage.
** {{dlc|a+}} Isaac can move to avoid the stomp.

== Notes ==
* The stomp is considered to be an explosion.
** {{dlc|nr}} Isaac can thus be immune to it with {{i|Host Hat}} or {{i|Pyromaniac}}
** {{dlc|r}} Although it remains an explosion for other purposes, these items no longer protect Isaac against the stomp.

== Strategy ==
* Since the foot is an explosion, it can be used as a substitute for {{e|Bomb}}s.
** It can break rocks and open doors to {{r|Secret Room}}s. {{dlc|r}} However, unlike bombs, it cannot destroy [[machines]] and {{m|Beggar}}s.
** In a room containing no enemies and a {{e|Shopkeeper}}, the foot will target it instead of Isaac.
* The foot deals 300 damage, enough to heavily weaken or even kill some bosses.
** All [[Chapter 1 (Bosses)|Chapter 1 bosses]] can be one shot from full health with one use of '''II - The High Priestess''' (except {{e|The Fallen}} for its two phases).

== Synergies ==
* {{I|Tarot Cloth|r}}: Another foot strikes down shortly after the first.
** {{I|Tarot Cloth|r}} + {{i|Blank Card}} + {{i|Car Battery|n}} : No extra effect, only two feet are spawned.

== Interactions ==
* {{I|Tarot Cloth|nr}}: No effect.
* {{I|Stop Watch|r}}: Even though it's not visible, it makes the foot stomp twice, dealing 600 damage.
** {{I|Stop Watch|r}} + {{I|Tarot Cloth|r}}: A maximum of 1200 damage can be dealt.

